    "q-86822": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86822",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-1)^{2}+(0-(-1))^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(1-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
