    "q-139472": {
      "dom_id": "step-q139472",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-1))^{2}+(2-(-1))^{2}+(5-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{27} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
