    "q-139513": {
      "dom_id": "step-q139513",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{24}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9}\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}})≈{24.09}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle.",
